var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/#Library-API","page":"Library API","text":"The exported names, and SshDataBridge.main, which is public but not exported.","title":"Library API"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Configuration","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Actions","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Actions"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Results-and-errors","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Results and errors"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Command-line-driver","page":"Library API","text":"","title":"Command-line driver"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.load_config","page":"Library API","text":"load_config(path::AbstractString)::BridgeConfig\n\nRead, parse, and validate the TOML configuration file at path. Every failure is reported as ArgumentError: a missing or unreadable file, a path that cannot be inspected, a file that grants any permission to group or others (it holds passwords; use mode 600), a TOML syntax error, and every validation failure. A syntax error is reported by its kind and line number only: the offending line may be a password line and is never printed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.load_config"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.parse_config","page":"Library API","text":"parse_config(dict::AbstractDict; config_dir::AbstractString=pwd())::BridgeConfig\n\nBuild a validated BridgeConfig from a parsed TOML dictionary. Every table is checked for unknown keys and every value for its expected type. [push].local_source_dir, [pull].local_destination_root, and the target keys name, host, and remote_dir are mandatory, password with auth = \"password\" (the default); every other key has a default or, as port and user, is left to ~/.ssh/config when absent. Relative local paths are resolved against config_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.parse_config"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.BridgeConfig","page":"Library API","text":"BridgeConfig\n\nComplete configuration: global transport options, push and pull parameters, and the non-empty list of targets. Target names must be unique, because each one names the local harvest directory of its target and two targets harvested concurrently into the same directory would overwrite each other's results. Two targets on the same host and port must not have overlapping remote directories, equal or one inside the other, because a project purge of one would remove the output of the other before it is harvested, and both would be deployed into one tree. The rule does not depend on purge_scope. Hosts are compared as node_key describes, IP addresses by value, with port 22 for a target whose port ~/.ssh/config decides. This is the lexical check on the configured values; it concerns hosts, not storage, and does not recognize an sshconfig alias and the name it stands for, two names or addresses of one machine, nodes that mount one filesystem, or a symbolic link or bind mount on the node. The command-line driver repeats it on the configuration that ssh evaluates for every target (see [`checkendpointoverlaps](@ref)), and the ownership marker (see [claimscript](@ref), [purge_script`](@ref)) covers nodes that share storage. The functions that take a single target act on the target they are given.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.BridgeConfig"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.GlobalOptions","page":"Library API","text":"GlobalOptions\n\nTransport parameters shared by all targets.\n\nFields\n\nconnect_timeout::Int: SSH connection timeout in seconds.\nstrict_host_key_checking::String: default host key policy (\"accept-new\", \"yes\", \"no\").\ncompress::Bool: whether rsync compresses in flight (-z).\nbandwidth_limit::Int: bandwidth cap in KiB/s per transfer (rsync --bwlimit); 0 means unlimited.\nserver_alive_interval::Int: seconds of silence from the server after which ssh sends a keepalive request (ServerAliveInterval); 0 leaves keepalive to the ssh client configuration.\nserver_alive_count_max::Int: unanswered keepalive requests after which ssh drops the connection (ServerAliveCountMax).\n\nssh abandons a connection after server_alive_interval * (server_alive_count_max + 1) seconds without an answer from the server, 60 s with the defaults, so the transfer or remote command fails instead of blocking. A session that runs through an existing master connection (ControlMaster) is kept alive by the master, whose own options govern; these two fields do not reach it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.GlobalOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.PushOptions","page":"Library API","text":"PushOptions\n\nParameters of the push action.\n\nFields\n\nlocal_source_dir::String: local project directory to deploy; mandatory in the configuration.\nexcludes::Vector{String}: rsync exclude patterns.\nrequire_clean_git::Bool: abort when the local git working tree has uncommitted changes.\nuse_gitignore::Bool: honor the .gitignore rules of the source tree during deployment.\nincludes::Vector{String}: rsync include patterns applied before the .gitignore filter, re-admitting paths the deployed project ignores; excludes take precedence. Empty by default.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.PushOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.PullOptions","page":"Library API","text":"PullOptions\n\nParameters of the pull action.\n\nFields\n\nlocal_destination_root::String: local root under which one directory per target is created; mandatory in the configuration. It also holds the rsync logs of every target, see transfer_log_path.\noutput_subdir::String: default output directory relative to each target's remote_dir.\nincludes::Vector{String}: rsync include patterns; empty means everything.\nexcludes::Vector{String}: rsync exclude patterns.\ncollision_strategy::Symbol: :resume, :backup, or :abort when the local directory exists.\nclean_remote_after_pull::Bool: purge the remote directory after a verified harvest.\npurge_scope::Symbol: directory removed by a purge: :project (the whole base directory, the default) or :output (the output directory only).\n\nclean_remote_after_pull cannot be combined with includes: a purge after a harvest narrowed by include patterns would destroy the files the filter left behind.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.PullOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.BridgeTarget","page":"Library API","text":"BridgeTarget\n\nA remote compute node and the layout of its campaign directory.\n\nFields\n\nname::String: unique label; it also names the local harvest directory.\nhost::String: DNS hostname, ssh_config Host alias, IPv4 address, or IPv6 literal.\nport::Union{Nothing, Int}: SSH daemon port in 1:65535; nothing leaves it to ~/.ssh/config.\nuser::Union{Nothing, String}: remote user name; nothing leaves it to ~/.ssh/config or the local account name.\nauth::Symbol: :password (the password is fed to sshpass) or :key (no secret; ssh authenticates by agent, identity file, certificate, or an existing master connection, as ~/.ssh/config provides).\npassword::Union{Nothing, String}: remote password of a password target, nothing for a key target; never printed by show.\nidentity_file::Union{Nothing, String}: private key of a key target, or a public key selecting an agent key, stored with a leading ~/ expanded (-i <path> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes).\nproxy_jump::Union{Nothing, String}: jump-host specification of a key target (-J), or \"none\" (any target; accepted in any letter case and stored as \"none\") to connect directly whatever ~/.ssh/config routes (-o ProxyCommand=none).\nremote_dir::String: absolute base directory of the campaign on the remote host.\noutput_subdir::String: output directory relative to remote_dir (default \"output\").\nstrict_host_key_checking::Union{String, Nothing}: optional host key policy override.\n\nremote_dir and output_subdir are stored normalized: . segments, repeated slashes, and trailing slashes are removed on construction, so that every command names the directory in one spelling. An output_subdir that is . itself stays ., the base directory.\n\nConstructors\n\nBridgeTarget(name, host; remote_dir, port=nothing, user=nothing, auth=:password,\n             password=nothing, identity_file=nothing, proxy_jump=nothing,\n             output_subdir=\"output\", strict_host_key_checking=nothing)\nBridgeTarget(name, host, port, user, password, remote_dir, output_subdir=\"output\",\n             strict_host_key_checking=nothing)\n\nThe positional form builds a password target. Every field is checked by validate_bridge_target_fields.\n\nExamples\n\nBridgeTarget(\"node01\", \"node01.cluster.example\", 22, \"researcher\", \"secret\",\n             \"/home/researcher/campaign\")\nBridgeTarget(\"cluster\", \"hpc\"; auth=:key, remote_dir=\"/scratch/researcher/campaign\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.BridgeTarget"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.probe_target","page":"Library API","text":"probe_target(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::ProbeResult\n\nCheck SSH reachability of target, the presence of rsync on the remote host, and the existence of the base and output directories. Connection, authentication, and spawn failures are reported through the result, never thrown; only a key target whose prerequisites fail (check_key_target_prerequisites) raises their ArgumentError when its command is built. A key target refused with Permission denied, or whose route raised a prompt (see prompt_refusal_environment), gets a hint in the message: no prompt is allowed, so the key must be in the agent, or a master connection must be open when the host asks for a second factor. A key target that fails with Host key verification failed, or whose route asked to confirm a host key, gets one as well: the confirmation cannot be answered, and strict_host_key_checking is not passed on to jump hosts, whose host-key policy comes from ~/.ssh/config. Both hints name the interactive command of interactive_ssh_command.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.probe_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.probe_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"probe_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig)::Vector{ProbeResult}\n\nProbe every configured target concurrently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.probe_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.push_target","page":"Library API","text":"push_target(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::TransferResult\n\nDeploy the local source tree to one target. The log directory (local_destination_root) is created first, then remote_dir on the node is created and claimed for the target (see claim_remote_directory), then rsync runs; the first step that fails ends the push with a failed result. A directory that another target has claimed refuses the push. On success the message gives the number of files and bytes transferred and the log path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.push_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"push_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nDeploy the local source tree to all configured targets concurrently. The source tree must exist, otherwise ArgumentError is thrown; when config.push.require_clean_git is set, it must also be a clean git working tree. Both checks run in dry-run mode as well.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.pull_target","page":"Library API","text":"pull_target(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false,\n            clean_remote::Bool=config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull)::TransferResult\n\nHarvest the output directory of one target into local_destination_root/<name>/. When clean_remote is set (by default it follows config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull), the directory selected by config.pull.purge_scope is purged afterwards, but only if verify_harvest finds the local copy complete. An incomplete harvest or a failed purge leaves the remote directory in place and fails the target, although the data were retrieved. With config.pull.includes set, a requested purge is refused with ArgumentError before any transfer, because files left behind by the filter would be destroyed. A local destination that cannot be prepared fails the target. Transferred files are appended to the log of transfer_log_path; the message gives the file count, the size, and the log path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.pull_all_targets","page":"Library API","text":"pull_all_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false,\n                 clean_remote::Bool=config.pull.clean_remote_after_pull)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nHarvest the remote output directories of all configured targets concurrently; clean_remote is checked against config.pull.includes before any target is contacted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_all_targets"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.clean_remote_target","page":"Library API","text":"clean_remote_target(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions;\n                    scope::Symbol=:project, dry_run::Bool=false)::TransferResult\n\nRemove the directory selected by scope (see purge_path) on the remote host with the script of purge_script, run under sh -c; the default removes the whole project directory. The path is checked with validate_remote_path_safety before any command is issued, against target.user or, when the target leaves the user to ~/.ssh/config, the user that resolve_endpoint evaluates. A refusal, by that check, by the evaluation, or by the script, is reported as a failed result. A purge that found no ownership marker of the target on the path says so in its message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.clean_remote_target"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.clean_all_remote_targets","page":"Library API","text":"clean_all_remote_targets(config::BridgeConfig; dry_run::Bool=false)::Vector{TransferResult}\n\nPurge the directory selected by config.pull.purge_scope on all configured targets concurrently.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.clean_all_remote_targets"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.ProbeResult","page":"Library API","text":"ProbeResult\n\nOutcome of probe on one target.\n\nFields\n\ntarget::BridgeTarget: the probed target.\nsuccess::Bool: SSH reachable and rsync present on the remote host.\nssh_ok::Bool: the probe command exited with status zero.\nrsync_ok::Bool: rsync is installed on the remote host.\nremote_dir_exists::Bool: the base directory exists.\nremote_output_dir_exists::Bool: the output directory exists.\nmessage::String: diagnostics, as printed in the summary.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ProbeResult"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.TransferResult","page":"Library API","text":"TransferResult\n\nOutcome of a push, pull, or clean action on one target.\n\nFields\n\ntarget::BridgeTarget: the affected target.\naction::Symbol: :push, :pull, or :clean.\nsuccess::Bool: whether the action completed with exit status zero.\nexit_code::Int: exit status of the underlying process, or -1 when no process produced one: the command could not be started, or the step was refused locally (unsafe purge path, unusable local directory, incomplete harvest).\nduration_seconds::Float64: wall-clock duration.\nmessage::String: outcome, as printed in the summary; never contains credentials.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.TransferResult"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.MissingBinaryError","page":"Library API","text":"MissingBinaryError(binaries::Vector{String})\n\nThrown when required system executables are not found in PATH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.MissingBinaryError"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.DirtyWorkingTreeError","page":"Library API","text":"DirtyWorkingTreeError(directory::String, entries::Vector{String})\n\nThrown when require_clean_git is enabled and the git working tree at directory has uncommitted changes; entries holds the git status --porcelain lines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.DirtyWorkingTreeError"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#SshDataBridge.main","page":"Library API","text":"main(args::AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}=ARGS; io::IO=stdout, err::IO=stderr)::Int\n\nRun the command-line driver (probe, push, pull, clean; see usage) and return the exit status instead of calling exit: 0 when every target succeeded, 1 on a usage, configuration, or precondition error, 2 when at least one target failed. Summary tables, and the usage text when --help is given, go to io; error messages, the usage text after a usage error, and log records go to err. scripts/run.jl is a thin wrapper around this function.\n\nExample\n\nexit(main([\"probe\", \"--config\", \"config.toml\"]))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.main"},{"category":"section","location":"configuration/#Configuration","page":"Configuration","text":"One TOML file describes a campaign. It may hold passwords in plain text, so load_config refuses a file that grants any permission to group or others. Create it from the template:\n\ninstall -m 600 config.example.toml config.toml\n\nUnknown keys and values of the wrong type are rejected before any node is contacted, and the message names the key. Relative local paths are resolved against the directory of the configuration file, and a leading ~ expands to the home directory. [push].local_source_dir, [pull].local_destination_root, and the target keys name, host, and remote_dir are mandatory, and password for a password target; every other key has a default. port and user may be left out, and ~/.ssh/config then decides; host may be one of its Host aliases.\n\nauth = \"password\" (the default) feeds the target's password to sshpass. auth = \"key\" supplies no secret: ssh authenticates with the agent, an identity file, a certificate, or an open master connection, and never prompts (BatchMode=yes, and for jump hosts an askpass program of the package that ends the ssh asking). A key target may name identity_file, passed as -i <path> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes, and proxy_jump, passed as ssh -J; a password target accepts neither, except proxy_jump = \"none\" (any letter case), which connects any target directly (-o ProxyCommand=none). Key targets need OpenSSH 8.4 or newer on the workstation, and a TMPDIR from which the askpass program can be executed (not mounted noexec). Options given on the ssh command line apply to the target, not to its jump hosts: strict_host_key_checking, connect_timeout, and identity_file do not reach a jump host, whose key, authentication, and timeout follow its own entry in ~/.ssh/config. A session through an existing master connection is kept alive by the master's own ServerAliveInterval, not by server_alive_interval.\n\nremote_dir and output_subdir must not contain .. segments or the characters *, ?, [, ], which rsync would expand on the node. Two targets on the same host and port must not share a remote_dir or nest one inside the other, whatever the purge_scope: a project purge of one would remove the output of the other before it is harvested, and both would be deployed into one tree. BridgeConfig checks the configured hosts; the command-line driver checks again, a dry run included, on the host name and port that ssh -G evaluates for every configured target as a command session (check_endpoint_overlaps). Host names are compared without case, IP addresses by the value the C library reads, as ssh does. Nodes that mount one filesystem, such as a shared /home on a cluster, are caught by the ownership marker that a push writes into remote_dir (claim_script): a push into a directory claimed by another target, or nested in or containing one, is refused (of two nested claims made at the same moment, at least one), and so is a purge that would remove another target's tree (purge_script). A numeric host with a field in octal or hexadecimal notation (192.0.2.012, 0xc0.0.2.10) is refused, and so is one that the C library does not read as an address (192.168.1.256, 2001:db8:10).","title":"Configuration"},{"category":"section","location":"configuration/#Template","page":"Configuration","text":"config.example.toml from the repository root lists every key with its constraints:\n\n# SshDataBridge configuration template. Install as config.toml with mode 600 and edit.\n\n[globals]\n# OpenSSH ConnectTimeout\nconnect_timeout = 10  # integer > 0; units: s\n\n# Host-key verification policy\nstrict_host_key_checking = \"accept-new\"  # one of: \"accept-new\" | \"yes\" | \"no\"\n\n# rsync compression (-z)\ncompress = true\n\n# rsync bandwidth limit per transfer\nbandwidth_limit = 0  # integer >= 0; units: KiB/s; 0 = unlimited\n\n# Server silence before ssh sends a keepalive request (ServerAliveInterval)\nserver_alive_interval = 15  # integer >= 0; units: s; 0 = ssh client configuration decides\n\n# Unanswered keepalive requests before ssh disconnects (ServerAliveCountMax)\nserver_alive_count_max = 3  # integer >= 1\n\n[push]\n# Local source directory deployed to every target (mandatory)\nlocal_source_dir = \"~/projects/sim_batch_01\"  # path relative to this config file or absolute; '~' expands\n\n# rsync exclude patterns for push (the default list)\nexcludes = [\n    \".git\",\n    \".github\",\n    \".vscode\",\n    \"*.swp\",\n    \"*~\",\n]\n\n# rsync include patterns applied before the .gitignore filter: deploy paths the project ignores\nincludes = []  # for example [\"/Manifest.toml\"] when every node runs the same Julia version\n\n# Apply the .gitignore rules of the source tree as rsync excludes (no '!' negations)\nuse_gitignore = true\n\n# Refuse to push from a working tree with uncommitted changes below local_source_dir\nrequire_clean_git = false\n\n[pull]\n# Local destination root: one subdirectory per target, plus the rsync logs (mandatory)\nlocal_destination_root = \"~/campaigns/sim_batch_01/harvest\"  # path relative to this config file or absolute; '~' expands\n\n# Output directory relative to remote_dir, for targets that do not set their own\noutput_subdir = \"output\"  # relative path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Harvest only files matching these patterns (empty = all files); excludes take precedence; not combinable with a purge\nincludes = []\n\n# rsync exclude patterns for pull (the default list)\nexcludes = [\n    \"*.tmp\",\n    \"*~\",\n]\n\n# Handling of an existing local directory of a target\ncollision_strategy = \"resume\"  # one of: \"resume\" | \"backup\" | \"abort\"\n\n# Purge the remote directory after a verified harvest (requires --yes on the CLI)\nclean_remote_after_pull = false\n\n# Remote directory removed by a purge\npurge_scope = \"project\"  # one of: \"project\" | \"output\"\n\n[[targets]]\n# Unique label (mandatory); names the local harvest directory and the rsync logs\nname = \"Cluster-Node-01\"  # starts with a letter or digit; letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'; at most 64 characters\n\n# Hostname, ssh_config Host alias, IPv4 address in decimal fields, or IPv6 literal without brackets\nhost = \"192.168.1.100\"\n\n# SSH daemon port (optional; when absent, ~/.ssh/config or 22)\nport = 22  # integer in [1, 65535]\n\n# Remote user name (optional; when absent, ~/.ssh/config or the local account name)\nuser = \"scientist\"  # letter or underscore, then letters, digits, '.', '_', '-'; at most 32 characters\n\n# Authentication method (optional; default \"password\")\nauth = \"password\"  # one of: \"password\" | \"key\"\n\n# Authentication password (password targets only)\npassword = \"example_password_1\"  # non-empty; no control characters\n\n# Base directory of the campaign on the node; no other target on the same host and port may use it or a directory inside it\nremote_dir = \"/home/scientist/campaigns/sim_batch_01\"  # absolute path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Remote output subdirectory relative to remote_dir (optional, defaults to [pull].output_subdir)\noutput_subdir = \"output\"  # relative path without '..' segments or '*', '?', '[', ']'\n\n# Host-key policy override (optional)\nstrict_host_key_checking = \"accept-new\"  # one of: \"accept-new\" | \"yes\" | \"no\"\n\n[[targets]]\nname = \"Cluster-Node-02\"\nhost = \"192.168.1.101\"\nport = 2222\nuser = \"engineer\"\npassword = \"example_password_2\"\nremote_dir = \"/home/engineer/campaigns/sim_batch_01\"\noutput_subdir = \"results\"\n\n[[targets]]\nname = \"Cluster\"\nhost = \"hpc\"\nauth = \"key\"\n\n# Key file passed as ssh -i with IdentitiesOnly (optional, key targets only)\n# absolute or starting with '~/'; no ', % or $; no group or other permission bits unless it ends in .pub\n# identity_file = \"~/.ssh/id_ed25519_hpc\"\n\n# Jump hosts passed as ssh -J (optional, key targets only)\nproxy_jump = \"admin@gateway.example.org\"  # [user@]host[:port] hops separated by ','; IPv6 in brackets in the last hop only; \"none\" (any target) = direct\n\nremote_dir = \"/scratch/scientist/campaigns/sim_batch_01\"\n\n\n","title":"Template"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/#Internals","page":"Internals","text":"The functions and constants behind the API: validators, command builders, process runners, and the purge helpers. None of them is exported, and any of them may change in a release.","title":"Internals"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.CliOptions","page":"Internals","text":"CliOptions\n\nParsed command line of the driver.\n\nFields\n\naction::Symbol: :help, :probe, :push, :pull, or :clean.\nconfig_path::String: configuration file to load.\ndry_run::Bool: print the commands without executing them.\nclean_remote::Bool: purge the remote directory after a verified harvest.\nconfirmed::Bool: --yes was given, confirming remote deletion.\ntargets::Vector{String}: names of the targets to act on; empty means every configured target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.CliOptions"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.SshEndpoint","page":"Internals","text":"SshEndpoint\n\nThe configuration that ssh -G evaluates for a target: the host it connects to, the port, the user, and the route.\n\nFields\n\nhostname::String: host name or address ssh connects to, after ssh_config HostName.\nport::Int: SSH daemon port.\nuser::String: remote user name.\nproxy_jump::Union{Nothing, String}: effective ProxyJump; nothing when none.\nproxy_command::Union{Nothing, String}: effective ProxyCommand; nothing when none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.SshEndpoint"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.assert_clean_git_tree-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"assert_clean_git_tree(dir::AbstractString)\n\nThrow MissingBinaryError when git is unavailable, ArgumentError when dir does not exist or is not inside a git working tree, and DirtyWorkingTreeError when the tree has uncommitted changes, including untracked files; only the tree below dir is examined. Returns nothing for a clean tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.assert_clean_git_tree"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_probe_script-Tuple{BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"build_probe_script(target::BridgeTarget)::String\n\nShell script executed on the remote host by probe_target. It reports whether rsync is installed and whether the base and output directories exist; every path is POSIX-quoted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_probe_script"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_pull_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_pull_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                   pull_opts::PullOptions, local_target_dir::AbstractString;\n                   log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing}=nothing)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the rsync invocation that retrieves the remote output directory of target into local_target_dir, with the filter rules of pull_filter_arguments, wrapped by target_command. The password of a password target is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it. With log_file, rsync appends the list of transferred files to that file, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_pull_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_push_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PushOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"build_push_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                   push_opts::PushOptions;\n                   log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing}=nothing)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the rsync invocation that deploys the local source tree to target, with the filter rules of push_filter_arguments, wrapped by target_command. The password of a password target is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it. With log_file, rsync appends the list of transferred files to that file, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_push_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_ssh_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_ssh_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                  remote_command::AbstractString)::Cmd\n\nConstruct the ssh -n ... invocation that executes remote_command on target, with the options of ssh_options, wrapped by target_command: a password target runs sshpass -d 0 ssh -n ..., and the password is not part of the command; run_authenticated supplies it through standard input at execution time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_ssh_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_ssh_rsh_string-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"build_ssh_rsh_string(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::String\n\nConstruct the remote-shell string passed to rsync -e, with the options of ssh_options; the keepalive among them ends a stalled transfer with a non-zero exit status instead of blocking it. rsync splits the string on spaces and honours quotes, so every word that contains a space or a \" is wrapped in single quotes; a single quote cannot occur, since validation refuses it in identity_file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_ssh_rsh_string"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.build_verification_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"build_verification_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions,\n                           pull_opts::PullOptions,\n                           local_target_dir::AbstractString)::Cmd\n\nThe harvest of build_pull_command repeated as a dry run: --dry-run transfers nothing, --itemize-changes prints one line per item that still differs between the remote output directory and local_target_dir. Without --stats and --log-file, standard output is empty exactly when nothing the filter rules admit differs; files matching excludes are not compared.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.build_verification_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_endpoint_overlaps-Tuple{AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}, AbstractVector{SshDataBridge.SshEndpoint}}","page":"Internals","text":"check_endpoint_overlaps(targets::AbstractVector{BridgeTarget},\n                        endpoints::AbstractVector{SshEndpoint})\n\nRepeat the overlap rule of BridgeConfig on the configuration that ssh evaluates: endpoints[i] belongs to targets[i]. Two targets whose endpoints have the same node_key of host name and port must not have overlapping remote directories, so that an ssh_config alias and the name it stands for, or a port that only ~/.ssh/config sets, cannot hide two targets on one node. Throws ArgumentError for the first such pair, DimensionMismatch when the lengths differ.\n\nThe route (ProxyJump, ProxyCommand) is deliberately not part of the key: two routes to one machine must not pass. Two machines with one private name behind different gateways are refused as well; this false refusal is the safe error, and distinct remote directories avoid it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_endpoint_overlaps"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_key_target_prerequisites-Tuple{AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}}","page":"Internals","text":"check_key_target_prerequisites(targets::AbstractVector{BridgeTarget})\n\nWhen a key target is among targets, require what every command of a key target rests on: OpenSSH 8.4 or newer (check_openssh_version) and a prompt-refusal program that runs (prompt_refusal_program); throws their ArgumentError otherwise. Part of check_local_binaries, and run on its own by the dry runs of push_all_targets, pull_all_targets, and clean_all_remote_targets, which need no binaries but still build the commands.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_key_target_prerequisites"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_local_binaries-Tuple{AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}}","page":"Internals","text":"check_local_binaries(targets::AbstractVector{BridgeTarget})\n\nVerify that ssh and rsync are available in PATH, and sshpass as well when a password target is among targets. Throws MissingBinaryError naming the missing binaries otherwise. When a key target is among targets, ssh must be OpenSSH 8.4 or newer, whose SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE keeps every prompt off the terminal (see prompt_refusal_environment), and prompt_refusal_program must be able to run; an older or unidentified client, or a program that cannot be executed, is refused with an ArgumentError.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_local_binaries"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_openssh_version-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"check_openssh_version()\n\nThrow an ArgumentError unless the ssh in PATH reports OpenSSH 8.4 or newer, the first release that honours SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE, on which the prompt refusal of key targets rests.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_openssh_version"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.check_prompt_refusal_program-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"check_prompt_refusal_program(path::AbstractString)\n\nRun the prompt-refusal program at path in its self-test mode, two arguments, which ssh never passes, and throw an ArgumentError unless it exits 0: ssh answers a prompt with an empty string when it cannot execute the program, for instance from a file system mounted noexec, which is the empty password the program exists to prevent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.check_prompt_refusal_program"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.claim_remote_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"claim_remote_directory(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)\n\nCreate target.remote_dir on the node and claim it for target with the script of claim_script. Returns (; success, exitcode, stderr); exit code 97 means that the directory belongs to another target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.claim_remote_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.claim_script-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"claim_script(remote_dir::AbstractString, name::AbstractString)::String\n\nOne-line POSIX shell script, run under sh -c, that creates remote_dir with mkdir -p and claims it for the target name through the ownership marker remote_dir/.sshdatabridge-target, which holds the name of the target. An absent marker is written to a temporary file named after the node and the shell's process ID, then hard-linked into place; the link is atomic and fails when the marker exists, also over NFS, where O_EXCL is not reliable on every server (open(2)). Of two concurrent claims of one directory exactly one marker is written, and both read it back rather than trust the status of ln, which NFS can report as failed after a lost reply. The physical location of the directory is resolved, and the claim is refused when a marker of another target lies in any ancestor or anywhere below it, so that a directory nested in the tree of another target is caught as well. That check runs before the marker is written and, by a claim whose link created the marker (the marker and its temporary file are one inode, which holds after a lost NFS reply as well), again afterwards: of two concurrent claims of nested directories each writes its own marker before its second check, so at least one of them sees the other's marker, removes its own, and refuses (both may refuse). A claim that found the marker in place, or lost the link to a concurrent claim of the same name, never removes it. The script exits 0 when the marker names name, 1 when the directory or the marker cannot be created, entered, or read (a file system without hard links included), and 97 when the marker, or one above or below the directory, names another target: the nodes share storage, or two targets name one directory or nested ones. The refusal states its reason on standard error. remote_dir and name are POSIX-quoted.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.claim_script"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.command_string-Tuple{Cmd}","page":"Internals","text":"command_string(cmd::Cmd)::String\n\nRender the argument vector of cmd as a POSIX-shell-quoted string. The environment of cmd is not rendered, so the result is safe to print or log.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.command_string"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.config_file_present-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"config_file_present(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path names a regular file. A path that cannot be inspected, because a directory on it is not searchable or it ends in a loop of symbolic links, raises ArgumentError with the reason.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.config_file_present"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.default_config_path-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"default_config_path()::String\n\nconfig.toml next to Project.toml of the package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.default_config_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.drain-Tuple{Pipe}","page":"Internals","text":"drain(pipe::Pipe)::Task\n\nClose the write end of pipe that the parent holds and return a task that reads the pipe to end-of-file as a String. To be called once the child has been started.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.drain"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.execute-Tuple{IO, Symbol, BridgeConfig, Bool, Bool}","page":"Internals","text":"execute(io::IO, action::Symbol, config::BridgeConfig, dry_run::Bool,\n        clean_remote::Bool)::Bool\n\nRun action and print its summary table to io; returns whether every target succeeded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.execute"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.exit_status-Tuple{Base.Process}","page":"Internals","text":"exit_status(process::Base.Process)::Int\n\nExit status of a finished process: its exit code, or 128 + signal when a signal terminated it, which Julia otherwise reports as exit code 0.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.exit_status"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.expand_identity_file-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"expand_identity_file(path::AbstractString, context::AbstractString)::String\n\nExpand a leading ~ of path to the home directory, as expanduser does. A path that starts with ~ followed by anything but / (~user/...) is refused with an ArgumentError naming the key and, through context, the target, since only the own home directory is expanded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.expand_identity_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_bytes-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"format_bytes(n::Integer)::String\n\nRender a byte count with a binary prefix and one decimal: 512 B, 1.5 KiB, 5.1 MiB.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_bytes"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_probe_table-Tuple{IO, Vector{ProbeResult}}","page":"Internals","text":"format_probe_table(io::IO, results::Vector{ProbeResult})\n\nPrint the probe results to io: one block per target, then a tally of the targets that are ready (reachable, with rsync installed). Fields that depend on a successful ssh command read unknown when it failed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_probe_table"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.format_transfer_table-Tuple{IO, Vector{TransferResult}, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"format_transfer_table(io::IO, results::Vector{TransferResult}, action::Symbol)\n\nPrint the outcome of a push, pull, or clean action to io: one line per target with its status, exit code, and duration, the message beneath it, then a tally.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.format_transfer_table"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_control_characters-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_control_characters(text::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether text contains an ASCII control character (0x00 to 0x1f, or 0x7f).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_control_characters"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_non_decimal_address_field-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_non_decimal_address_field(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host is a numeric address with a field in octal or hexadecimal notation (192.0.2.012, 0xc0.0.2.10), which the C library accepts and reads by another value than the decimal one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_non_decimal_address_field"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_parent_segment-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_parent_segment(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path contains a .. segment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_parent_segment"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.has_rsync_wildcards-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"has_rsync_wildcards(path::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether path contains *, ?, [, or ]. rsync would expand them on the node, so that a transfer could act on another directory than the one named, while the purge removes the path as written.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.has_rsync_wildcards"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.interactive_ssh_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"interactive_ssh_command(target::BridgeTarget; master::Bool=false)::String\n\nThe ssh command line, POSIX-quoted, with which the user reaches target interactively along the same route as the package: its port, identity file, and jump hosts, without BatchMode. With master = true it opens a background connection (-fN), which serves later connections when ~/.ssh/config sets ControlMaster and ControlPath for the host. Used in the hints of probe_target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.interactive_ssh_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.is_numeric_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_numeric_host(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host can only be an IP address: it contains a :, or every label is a number, with or without a trailing dot. An all-numeric name is not a DNS name (RFC 3696, section 2).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.is_numeric_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.is_valid_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_valid_host(host::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether host is a syntactically valid DNS hostname, sshconfig Host alias, IPv4 address, or IPv6 literal (without square brackets, which ssh does not strip from user@host). Names and aliases are dot-separated labels of letters, digits, `, and interior hyphens; a leading-never matches, so that a host is never read as anssh` option.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.is_valid_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.is_valid_proxy_jump-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_valid_proxy_jump(spec::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether spec is a jump-host specification accepted for ssh -J: one or more [user@]host[:port] hops separated by commas, an IPv6 host enclosed in square brackets, or exactly none, which disables a ProxyJump or ProxyCommand set in ~/.ssh/config. Each user must be a valid account name, each host a valid host name, alias, or IPv4 address (an IPv6 literal only in brackets), and each port lie in 1:65535. Empty specifications and hops, control characters, and ssh:// URIs are refused. A bracketed IPv6 host is accepted in the last hop only: OpenSSH inserts the hops before the last unquoted into the command it builds for the last jump host and runs that command with the user's shell ($SHELL -c), which would read the brackets as a glob pattern. The other characters a hop admits (letters, digits, ., _, -, @, :, ,) are not special to the usual shells.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.is_valid_proxy_jump"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.keepalive_options-Tuple{GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"keepalive_options(globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nssh options that drop a connection the server has stopped answering: -o ServerAliveInterval=<s> -o ServerAliveCountMax=<n>. Empty when server_alive_interval is 0, so that the ssh client configuration applies; an explicit ServerAliveInterval=0 on the command line would override it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.keepalive_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.map_targets-Union{Tuple{R}, Tuple{Any, AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}, Type{R}}} where R","page":"Internals","text":"map_targets(f, targets::AbstractVector{BridgeTarget}, ::Type{R})::Vector{R}\n\nApply f to every target on its own task and return the results in target order. Every task runs to completion before an exception of any of them propagates, so a failure on one target neither interrupts the others nor leaves a remote command unfinished.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.map_targets"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.node_key-Tuple{AbstractString, Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"node_key(host::AbstractString, port::Integer)::Tuple{String, Int}\n\nIdentity of an ssh endpoint when targets are compared: the host and the port. A host name is taken in lower case without a trailing dot. An IP address is taken by its value (see numeric_address), so that its spellings give one key: IPv6 groups written in full or compressed, in either letter case, an IPv4 address mapped into IPv6, a shortened IPv4 form. A name and its address, or two names of one machine, are not recognized as the same node.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.node_key"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.numeric_address-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"numeric_address(host::AbstractString)::Union{Tuple{Int, UInt128}, Nothing}\n\nThe address of a numeric host as the C library reads it, and therefore as ssh connects to it: (6, value) for an IPv6 literal (inet_pton), (4, value) for an IPv4 address, shortened forms such as 192.0.522 included (inet_aton). An IPv4 address mapped into IPv6 (::ffff:a.b.c.d) is returned as that IPv4 address. nothing when host is not numeric or the C library does not read it as an address.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.numeric_address"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.openssh_version-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"openssh_version()::Union{Nothing, VersionNumber}\n\nVersion of the ssh client in PATH as ssh -V reports it (OpenSSH_9.9p2, ... gives v\"9.9\"), or nothing when ssh cannot be run or is not OpenSSH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.openssh_version"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.optional_value-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Type{T}, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"optional_value(table::AbstractDict, key::AbstractString, ::Type{T}, context) where {T}\n\nReturn table[key] checked to be a T, or nothing when the key is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.optional_value"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.parse_arguments-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_arguments(args; default_config=default_config_path())::CliOptions\n\nParse the command line of the driver. --help or -h anywhere, or an empty command line, selects the :help action. Actions and options match exactly. Throws ArgumentError for an unknown action, an unrecognized option, --config without a path or given twice, --clean-remote with an action other than pull, or --yes with an action other than pull or clean. --target NAME may be repeated and restricts the action to the named targets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.parse_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.parse_ssh_config-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_ssh_config(text::AbstractString)::SshEndpoint\n\nRead the output of ssh -G: one key value line per option, the key in lower case. The first occurrence of a key counts. hostname, port, and user are required, and the port must be an integer in 1:65535; proxyjump and proxycommand absent or none give nothing. Throws ArgumentError otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.parse_ssh_config"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.paths_overlap-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"paths_overlap(a::AbstractString, b::AbstractString)::Bool\n\nWhether two normalized absolute paths name the same directory or one lies below the other. The comparison is lexical and does not follow symbolic links.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.paths_overlap"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.prepare_local_pull_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget, PullOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"prepare_local_pull_directory(target::BridgeTarget, pull_opts::PullOptions)::String\n\nResolve and create the local destination directory of target according to the collision strategy: :resume keeps an existing directory, :backup renames it with a #n suffix before creating a fresh one, and :abort throws an ErrorException.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.prepare_local_pull_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.prompt_refusal_environment-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"prompt_refusal_environment()::Vector{Pair{String, String}}\n\nEnvironment of the commands of a key target: SSH_ASKPASS set to prompt_refusal_program and SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=force (OpenSSH ≥ 8.4, which check_local_binaries requires for key targets). BatchMode does not reach the ssh that ProxyJump starts for a jump host, which receives only -l, -p, -F, and -v; it inherits the environment, however. Every prompt anywhere on the route therefore goes to the program, which reports it on standard error and terminates the ssh that asked, so that the connection fails at once, without reading the terminal and without sending an empty answer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.prompt_refusal_environment"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.prompt_refusal_program-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"prompt_refusal_program()::String\n\nPath of an executable copy of the prompt-refusal script, written on first use into a private temporary directory that Julia removes at exit, and written again when the copy has gone. A new copy must pass check_prompt_refusal_program, and the ssh in PATH check_openssh_version; throws the ArgumentError of either otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.prompt_refusal_program"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.pull_endpoint_arguments-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions, PullOptions, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"pull_endpoint_arguments(target, globals, pull_opts, local_target_dir)::Vector{String}\n\nRemote shell, filter rules, source, and destination of a harvest; shared by the transfer and by its verification pass so that both always compare the same file set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_endpoint_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.pull_filter_arguments-Tuple{PullOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"pull_filter_arguments(pull_opts::PullOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nrsync filter rules of a harvest. The ownership marker at the root of the transfer (see claim_script) is excluded first, so that it is never harvested nor compared by the verification pass; with output_subdir = \".\" the output directory is the project directory. Exclude patterns come next and therefore take precedence. When include patterns are given, the harvest is narrowed to files matching one of them: every directory is entered (--include=*/), the include patterns follow, a final --exclude=* drops everything else, and --prune-empty-dirs omits directories left without files. Include rules alone would not narrow anything, because rsync transfers every file that no rule excludes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.pull_filter_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.purge_path-Tuple{BridgeTarget, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"purge_path(target::BridgeTarget, scope::Symbol)::String\n\nRemote directory removed by a purge of target: the output directory for scope == :output, the whole project directory for scope == :project.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.purge_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.purge_script-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"purge_script(path::AbstractString, name::AbstractString)::String\n\nOne-line POSIX shell script that removes path recursively on the node for the target name. It exits 0 when the path does not exist. It exits 98, deleting nothing, when the path is a symbolic link, whose removal would leave the deployed tree in place; when the path or the home directory of the account cannot be entered (a file, or a directory without search permission), so that their physical locations cannot be compared; and when the path is a directory that contains the home directory, which the lexical rules of validate_remote_path_safety cannot see. It also exits 98 when an ownership marker of another target (see claim_script) lies in the physical location of the path or in any of its ancestors, or anywhere below it. Without any marker of name on the path the purge proceeds and notes this on standard error (purge note:). Each refusal states its reason on standard error. path and name are POSIX-quoted, path without a trailing slash, so that the link test sees a link and not the directory behind it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.purge_script"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.push_filter_arguments-Tuple{PushOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"push_filter_arguments(push_opts::PushOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nrsync filter rules of a deployment, in precedence order: the ownership marker at the root of the source tree (see claim_script), which would otherwise replace the claim just made, then the exclude patterns, then the include patterns, then the dir-merge filter that applies the .gitignore of the source tree. rsync takes the first matching rule, so an exclude always wins and an include re-admits a path that .gitignore would drop (/Manifest.toml, for example).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.push_filter_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.reject_unknown_keys-Tuple{AbstractDict, Any, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"reject_unknown_keys(table::AbstractDict, allowed, context::AbstractString)\n\nThrow ArgumentError listing every key of table that is not in allowed, so that misspelled configuration keys fail before a run starts.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.reject_unknown_keys"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.remote_output_directory-Tuple{BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"remote_output_directory(target::BridgeTarget)::String\n\nAbsolute path of the output directory of target on the remote host, without a trailing slash. normpath keeps one when output_subdir ends in a . segment, and a purge of link/ would empty the directory behind a symbolic link that the purge script refuses.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.remote_output_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.remote_shell-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"remote_shell(script::AbstractString)::String\n\nWrap script as sh -c '<script>', so that it runs under a POSIX shell whatever the login shell of the remote account.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.remote_shell"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.required_value-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Type{T}, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"required_value(table::AbstractDict, key::AbstractString, ::Type{T}, context) where {T}\n\nReturn table[key] checked to be a T; throws ArgumentError if the key is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.required_value"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_endpoint-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_endpoint(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::SshEndpoint\n\nEvaluate the configuration of target with ssh_config_command and read it with parse_ssh_config. Throws ArgumentError naming the target when ssh exits with a non-zero status or its output cannot be read.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_endpoint"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_endpoints-Tuple{BridgeConfig}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_endpoints(config::BridgeConfig)::Vector{SshEndpoint}\n\nEvaluate the configuration of every target in order, one after the other, see resolve_endpoint. Throws MissingBinaryError when ssh is not in PATH, and ArgumentError for the first target whose configuration cannot be evaluated.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_endpoints"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_local_path-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_local_path(path::AbstractString, config_dir::AbstractString)::String\n\nExpand a leading ~ and resolve a relative path against config_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_local_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.resolve_target_policy-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_target_policy(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::String\n\nReturn the effective host key policy of target, honoring its override when present.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.resolve_target_policy"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.rsync_base_arguments-Tuple{GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"rsync_base_arguments(globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nLeading arguments shared by every rsync invocation: rsync, the archive and resumption flags, -s (--secluded-args), and the optional compression and bandwidth settings. target_command adds the sshpass prefix of a password target. With -s the remote path reaches the remote rsync through the protocol and not through the remote shell, which would split or expand it under rsync older than 3.2.4 or with RSYNC_OLD_ARGS set. -v is not among them: a transfer records its file list in a log file instead, see transfer_log_path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.rsync_base_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.rsync_host-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"rsync_host(host::AbstractString)::String\n\nReturn host in the form accepted by rsync endpoints: IPv6 literals are wrapped in square brackets, everything else is returned unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.rsync_host"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_authenticated-Tuple{Cmd, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"run_authenticated(cmd::Cmd, password::AbstractString)\n\nRun cmd, whose first words must be sshpass -d 0, feeding password followed by a newline through standard input so that the secret never appears in any process environment or argument vector. Returns (; exitcode, stdout, stderr) and throws nothing: a non-zero exit status is reported, a signal-terminated child reports 128 + signal, and a command that cannot be started reports -1 with the reason in stderr. Base.IOError raised while writing the password is ignored, because it only means the child exited before reading it (for example a refused connection).\n\nBoth streams are read to end-of-file. Buffers handed to pipeline are not enough on Julia 1.10, where wait returns when the child exits, not when its output has been copied, so that the output could be read incomplete or empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_authenticated"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_captured-Tuple{Cmd}","page":"Internals","text":"run_captured(cmd::Cmd)\n\nRun a command that needs no credentials, with standard input from devnull, capturing standard output and standard error, both read to end-of-file as in run_authenticated. Returns (; exitcode, stdout, stderr) and throws nothing: a non-zero exit status is reported, a signal-terminated child reports 128 + signal, and a command that cannot be started reports -1 with the reason in stderr.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_captured"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_driver-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:AbstractString}, IO, IO}","page":"Internals","text":"run_driver(args, io::IO, err::IO)::Int\n\nBody of main without the logger setup.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_driver"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.run_target-Tuple{Cmd, BridgeTarget}","page":"Internals","text":"run_target(cmd::Cmd, target::BridgeTarget)\n\nRun a command of target and return (; exitcode, stdout, stderr); the one place that decides how the command receives its credential. A password target runs through run_authenticated, which feeds the password to sshpass; a key target runs through run_captured, ssh authenticating without a secret from this package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.run_target"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.ssh_config_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"ssh_config_command(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::Cmd\n\nssh -G with the options of ssh_options, the destination of target, and the remote command sh -c true: ssh prints the configuration it would use and never connects, so the command needs neither sshpass nor the environment of prompt_refusal_environment. The remote command makes ssh evaluate the session as the commands of the package are evaluated, a command session, which Match sessiontype (OpenSSH 10.0) tells apart from an interactive one. A Match command block that tells the shell commands of the package from rsync's rsync --server is not seen. -o RemoteCommand=none keeps a RemoteCommand of the host's block from making the query fail (\"Cannot execute command-line and remote command\"); the commands of such a target still fail, that target alone.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ssh_config_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.ssh_options-Tuple{BridgeTarget, GlobalOptions}","page":"Internals","text":"ssh_options(target::BridgeTarget, globals::GlobalOptions)::Vector{String}\n\nssh options shared by the direct commands, the rsync transport, and ssh -G: the port when the target sets one, host-key policy, connection timeout, keepalive (see keepalive_options), then the authentication options of the target.\n\nA password target pins authentication to passwords. Public-key authentication is disabled and the preferred methods are keyboard-interactive and password, so that an agent holding many keys cannot exhaust the server's authentication attempts and an encrypted key cannot raise a passphrase prompt that sshpass does not answer; one password prompt is allowed.\n\nA key target sets BatchMode=yes, so that ssh fails instead of prompting, followed by -i <identity_file> -o IdentitiesOnly=yes and -J <proxy_jump> when these are set; everything else is left to ~/.ssh/config. proxy_jump = \"none\", the one value a password target admits, is passed as -o ProxyCommand=none, which overrides both a ProxyJump and a ProxyCommand of ~/.ssh/config (-J none overrides only the former).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.ssh_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.syntax_error_line-Tuple{Base.TOML.ParserError}","page":"Internals","text":"syntax_error_line(err::TOML.ParserError)::Int\n\nNumber of the line that showerror would print for err: the line that holds the position of the error in the source text. The line field of the parser is not used, because it is ahead by one whenever the last character read was a newline. It is the fallback, with 0, when the parser kept no source text.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.syntax_error_line"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.target_address-Tuple{AbstractString, Union{Nothing, Integer}, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"target_address(host::AbstractString, port::Union{Nothing, Integer},\n               user::Union{Nothing, AbstractString})::String\ntarget_address(target::BridgeTarget)::String\n\nEndpoint of a target as configured, for display: [user@]host[:port], each optional part omitted when ~/.ssh/config decides it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.target_address"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.target_command-Tuple{BridgeTarget, Vector{String}}","page":"Internals","text":"target_command(target::BridgeTarget, arguments::Vector{String})::Cmd\n\nCommand that runs arguments, which start with \"ssh\" or \"rsync\", for target: prefixed with sshpass -d 0 for a password target, which reads the password from standard input (see run_authenticated), with SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=never, since with prefer or force in the caller's environment ssh would ask an askpass program instead of the terminal that sshpass answers; with the environment of prompt_refusal_environment for a key target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.target_command"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.target_label-Tuple{AbstractString, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"target_label(host::AbstractString, user::Union{Nothing, AbstractString})::String\n\nDestination as ssh receives it: user@host, or host alone when user is nothing and ssh_config or the local account name supplies it. Used in messages and as the last argument of the ssh command.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.target_label"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_arguments-Tuple{Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_arguments(log_file::Union{AbstractString, Nothing})::Vector{String}\n\nArguments that distinguish a transfer from its verification pass: --stats, so that rsync prints its statistics block on standard output, and --log-file=<log_file> when a log file is given.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_arguments"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_log_path-Tuple{BridgeConfig, BridgeTarget, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_log_path(config::BridgeConfig, target::BridgeTarget, action::Symbol)::String\n\nLocal rsync log of action (:push or :pull) for target: <local_destination_root>/<name>.<action>.rsync.log. rsync appends to it, so the file accumulates every transfer of the campaign for that target: one timestamped line per transferred file and the statistics block of each run. Throws ArgumentError for any other action.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_log_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_statistics-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_statistics(stdout::AbstractString)\n\nParse the statistics block that rsync --stats prints: returns (; files, bytes), the number of regular files transferred and the total transferred file size in bytes, or nothing when either line is absent. Any thousands separator the locale inserts is ignored.\n\nExample\n\njulia> transfer_statistics(\"Number of regular files transferred: 1,234\\nTotal transferred file size: 5,368,709 bytes\\n\")\n(files = 1234, bytes = 5368709)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_statistics"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.transfer_summary-Tuple{AbstractString, Real, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"transfer_summary(verb::AbstractString, duration::Real, stdout::AbstractString,\n                 log_file::AbstractString)::String\n\nSuccess message of a transfer: \"<verb> successfully in <duration> s: <files> files, <size> transferred; log: <log_file>.\", or without the file count and size when transfer_statistics finds no statistics block in stdout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.transfer_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.typed_value-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Type{T}, Any, AbstractString}} where T","page":"Internals","text":"typed_value(table::AbstractDict, key::AbstractString, ::Type{T}, default, context) where {T}\n\nReturn table[key] if present, otherwise default, checking that the value is a T. A boolean is never accepted for a numeric T, although Bool <: Integer in Julia, so that port = true cannot silently become port 1. Throws ArgumentError naming context.key on a type mismatch.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.typed_value"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.usage-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"usage()::String\n\nThe command-line reference printed by --help and after a usage error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.usage"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_bridge_target_fields-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Union{Nothing, Integer}, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, Symbol, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}, AbstractString, AbstractString, Union{Nothing, AbstractString}}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_bridge_target_fields(name, host, port, user, auth, password, identity_file,\n                              proxy_jump, remote_dir, output_subdir,\n                              strict_host_key_checking)\n\nVerify every field of a remote target: name must be a valid directory name, host a hostname, sshconfig alias, or IP literal, port (when set) within 1:65535, user (when set) a POSIX user name, and auth one of :password or :key. A password target requires a non-empty password free of control characters, admits no `identityfile, and admitsproxyjumponly as\"none\", sincesshpasswould hand the password to a jump host that asks for one. A key target admits nopassword, anidentityfilethat passes [validateidentityfile](@ref), and aproxyjumpthat passes [isvalidproxyjump](@ref).remotedirmust be an absolute path,outputsubdira relative path, andstricthostkey_checkingone of the accepted policies. ThrowsArgumentError` on the first violation; error messages never include the password.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_bridge_target_fields"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_global_options-Tuple{Integer, AbstractString, Integer, Integer, Integer}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_global_options(connect_timeout::Integer, strict_host_key_checking::AbstractString,\n                        bandwidth_limit::Integer, server_alive_interval::Integer,\n                        server_alive_count_max::Integer)\n\nVerify the global transport parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_global_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_identity_file-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_identity_file(path::AbstractString, context::AbstractString)\n\nRequire path, already expanded by expand_identity_file, to name a key file that ssh opens as given and that the remote-shell string of rsync can carry: free of control characters, of single quotes, and of % and $, which ssh expands in an identity path (%d, ${HOME}) after the check made here, absolute, and a regular file. A private key must have no group or other permission bits, which ssh refuses for a key of its owner; a public key (.pub), which selects the key of an agent or a security token, is exempt. The file content is never read. Throws ArgumentError naming the violated condition, also when the path cannot be inspected; context names the target in the message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_identity_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_patterns-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_patterns(patterns::AbstractVector, key::AbstractString)\n\nRequire every rsync include or exclude pattern to be a non-empty string without control characters, and one that rsync takes as a pattern: it reads a leading + or - as an include or exclude rule of its own, and a lone ! as the instruction to drop every earlier rule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_patterns"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_pull_options-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Symbol, Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_pull_options(local_destination_root::AbstractString,\n                      output_subdir::AbstractString, collision_strategy::Symbol,\n                      purge_scope::Symbol)\n\nVerify the harvesting parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_pull_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_push_options-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_push_options(local_source_dir::AbstractString)\n\nVerify the deployment parameters. Throws ArgumentError on violation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_push_options"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_relative_subdirectory-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_relative_subdirectory(path::AbstractString, key::AbstractString,\n                               context::AbstractString)\n\nRequire a non-empty relative path without control characters, .. segments, or rsync wildcard characters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_relative_subdirectory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_remote_directory-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_remote_directory(path::AbstractString, key::AbstractString,\n                          context::AbstractString)\n\nRequire an absolute remote directory without control characters, .. segments, or rsync wildcard characters, other than the filesystem root in any spelling (/, //, /.). key and context name the offending parameter in the error message.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_remote_directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.validate_remote_path_safety-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_remote_path_safety(path::AbstractString, user::AbstractString)\n\nVerify that path may be removed recursively on a remote host. The path must be absolute, free of control characters and .. segments, at least two components deep, and neither the filesystem root, /root, /home, the home directory of user, nor located under a protected system directory (/usr, /etc, /var, ...). Throws ArgumentError otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.validate_remote_path_safety"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#SshDataBridge.verify_harvest-Tuple{BridgeTarget, BridgeConfig, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"verify_harvest(target::BridgeTarget, config::BridgeConfig,\n               local_target_dir::AbstractString)\n\nRun the verification pass of build_verification_command and return (; complete, detail). The harvest counts as complete only when the pass exits with status zero and prints nothing; any output line is an item that changed on the remote since the transfer (a job still writing, for example). detail explains an incomplete harvest and is empty otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"SshDataBridge.verify_harvest"},{"category":"section","location":"#SshDataBridge.jl","page":"Home","text":"Deploys a simulation code base to several remote compute nodes with rsync over ssh and later harvests their results, on all nodes in parallel. One TOML file describes the nodes and the paths.\n\nThe README covers the command line: the actions probe, push, pull, and clean, their options, the rules of a purge, and the security model. These pages hold the reference: the configuration file and the library API.","title":"SshDataBridge.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Requirements","page":"Home","text":"Linux workstation with the OpenSSH client (8.4 or newer for key targets) and rsync, and sshpass when the configuration holds a password target. Every remote node needs rsync as well, version 3.0 or newer on both sides. Julia 1.10 or later.","title":"Requirements"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"The package is not registered. Add it by URL:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/PaulGoG/SshDataBridge.jl\")\n\nTo use the command-line driver, clone the repository instead and run julia scripts/run.jl, as the README describes.","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Use-from-Julia","page":"Home","text":"Each action of the command line is a function that takes the loaded configuration and returns one result per target:\n\nusing SshDataBridge\n\nconfig = load_config(\"config.toml\")\n\nprobe_all_targets(config)                         # Vector{ProbeResult}\npush_all_targets(config; dry_run=true)            # Vector{TransferResult} holding the rsync commands\npull_all_targets(config)\nclean_all_remote_targets(config; dry_run=true)\n\nprobe_target, push_target, pull_target, and clean_remote_target act on a single target. SshDataBridge.main runs the command-line driver in process and returns its exit status:\n\nSshDataBridge.main([\"probe\", \"--config\", \"config.toml\"])\n\nThe library functions do not ask for confirmation. clean_remote_target purges when called, and pull_target purges after a verified harvest when clean_remote_after_pull is set. The --yes gate belongs to the command line. The rule against overlapping targets is checked when a BridgeConfig is built, on the configured hosts; the command-line driver repeats it on the hosts that ssh -G evaluates (resolve_endpoints, check_endpoint_overlaps), which a library caller runs itself. The functions that take a single target act on the target they are given.","title":"Use from Julia"}]
}
